  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>An essential point upfront</h2>
      <p>The Plaine des Maures is a national nature reserve managed by the SNPN. Its founding decree (no. 2009-754, article 16) says dogs must be kept on a leash, except in sectors and periods where the prefect regulates access. After the August 2021 fire, which swept through about half of the reserve (inspectorate report, 2022), a prefectural order of 10 September 2021 banned pedestrians from the reserve's routes; the Conservatoire d'espaces naturels PACA described it at the time as a ban "for one year". The order was the subject of an appeal ruled on by the Toulon administrative court on 30/03/2023. We have not found a text in force in 2026 saying whether the ban was lifted or extended: for access to the Var massifs, the SNPN refers visitors to the prefecture's website (risque-prevention-incendie.fr/var). As in the other Var massifs, access may also be restricted in summer for wildfire risk (annual prefectural order, cited by the Conservatoire du littoral for 21 June to 20 September).</p>

      <h2>The Sentier de la Résilience</h2>
      <p>The "Sentier de la Résilience" is a 3.5 km educational trail with 10 information panels, built by the SNPN and presented at the regional nature reserves network assembly in 2025; it starts at the first Lac des Escarcets car park (Le Cannet-des-Maures). Keep your dog on a leash and stay on the marked trail, with no collecting of species or minerals. The ground is scrubland, sandy and rocky in places, with cork oaks and umbrella pines giving some shade. Lac des Escarcets itself (11 ha, reed beds, Natura 2000 site) is not suitable for dog swimming: water and boating activities are banned in the reserve (article 20 of the decree).</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> current access to the reserve (the 2021 order was not found in an up-to-date version) and any summer ban linked to wildfire risk. Sources read on 06/11/2026: decree 2009-754 (Légifrance), the reserve page on snpn.com, CEN PACA (28/09/2021), Toulon administrative court ruling (30/03/2023), RREN 2025 plenary assembly.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: stay on the marked trail, keep your dog on a leash, and check access with the SNPN (rnn.plainedesmaures@snpn.fr) before you come; the ecosystem is still recovering from the fire.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Le Cannet-des-Maures and the villages of the Massif des Maures are nearby, to extend the day after this short, guided walk. In this same central Var area, <a href="/en/fiche-lac-carces">Lac de Carcès</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-riviere-argens">Argens River</a> offer other waterways less than 30 minutes away, and the <a href="/en/fiche-activite-club-canin-dracenois">Club Canin Dracénois</a> in Draguignan can round out the outing with guided activities.</p>
